Cell["\<\
Use this interface when another calculation has already produced the symmetry \
matrices. It is deliberately separate from init: basisFunctions, \
SiteLocalData, and GenerateSymmetryGroup are not accepted.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b7cb3880-aa63-420c-b215-8dd2f095db7a"],

Cell["\<\
symminformation must contain the complete finite group in a fixed order, and \
repinformation must contain one exact unitary matrix for every operation in \
exactly that order.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d359bd1b-ac42-4911-ac71-5e81e235e3ec"],

Cell["\<\
For the supported continuous case, one pure-internal C_infinity generator may \
be supplied together with the finite matrices through the documented Discrete \
and Continuous form. The continuous operation constrains the local states but \
does not move atoms or generate bond orbits.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2e19df44-2d11-49a5-b151-8c14048d9a0a"],

Cell["\<\
By default initfromrep finds the first 10 complete bond shells. If a model \
needs a farther neighbour hopping, choose a larger InitialBondShells value \
and run initfromrep again; symham does not search for new bonds.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5be61248-1726-46d5-bc75-e64c3ae142ad"],

Cell["\<\
Every call to initfromrep starts a new model. If the ordered group and \
representation data are inconsistent, initialization fails and MagneticTB \
does not continue with the preceding model.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"dc0e5dbe-3b79-4a2e-a3f6-600521956543"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "8f8a3ccf-5c41-4020-b906-83548c409b36"], "lattice", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"a", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "a"}], "/", "2"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "3", "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"a", "/", "2"}]}], ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "c"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], Cell["\<\
Primitive direct-lattice vectors stored by rows. The numerical lattice \
obtained after lattpar must be real and nonsingular.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"c2cd6529-2666-4801-9598-64cd562be330"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "7f2cab87-afdb-4c24-80c5-22b966344f92"], "lattpar", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"a", "->", "1"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"c", "->", "3"}]}], "}"}], Cell["\<\
Replacement rules assigning every symbolic lattice parameter used by lattice.\
\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"87970a14-1dce-463e-9da9-a3f281654c25"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "2ea1aabc-a52d-4223-9ff8-845bd5055918"], "wyckoffposition", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"2", "/", "3"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "3"}], ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "}"}], Cell["\<\
One fractional seed and magnetic moment per Wyckoff orbit; the orbit order \
must match repinformation and orbitalLabels.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"ed23ea9c-0bd4-4b4a-8ed2-25a37132dce5"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "9ec2de29-b554-45b9-924f-e53cb06ca2ba"], "symminformation", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<1\>\"", ",", 
       RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", "\"\<F\>\""}], "}"}], 
     "}"}], Cell["\<\
A complete, already closed, ordered finite magnetic or spin-space group. One \
additional pure-internal C_infty Association is allowed.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"679b2119-5ee9-4413-9388-766ad066c772"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "5d5ecdd4-79d3-4efe-8cf2-4754fae7b3b3"], "repinformation", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}], "}"}], "}"}], Cell["\<\
Exact representation matrices in exactly the finite-group order. Use the \
documented Discrete/Continuous Association for C_infty.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"a050c3b4-7ffe-4dc4-bfab-5b7462cd1279"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "37935f8b-ad99-4dd6-ad3e-008bcb959f99"], "orbitalLabels", "Automatic", 
    Cell["\<\
Names used to display the coordinates of the supplied representation. \
Automatic uses orb1, orb2, and so on; these labels do not change the matrices.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"b218f5c7-ed89-4400-8449-6151fd94ce39"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "6ed9df8b-ab55-46ec-9a15-669db803e7de"], "InitialBondShells", "10", 
    Cell["\<\
Number of complete bond shells prepared during initialization. Shell 1 \
contains onsite terms; shell 2 is the first nonzero-distance neighbour shell.\
\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"2356407a-2cc1-43aa-9f32-8812a90e4115"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "3c7515a9-e75e-4076-9b9b-6fc4e92aac7a"], 
    "RepresentationMode", "\"\<DirectProduct\>\"", Cell["\<\
Use \"DirectProduct\" when repinformation already gives the full local \
action, or \"Induced\" when it gives the representation of a reference site's \
symmetry group.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"392f58cc-f409-40e8-966e-4ac391cd3a97"]}
  },
